              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for an impression left on you, then the Mandarin for to give an account of."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 去世",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "去世 — qùshì — \"to pass away\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "他的外公去年去世了 tā de wàigōng qùnián qùshì le — His grandfather died last year."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 世 (shì) — five strokes: a long bar; two verticals through it; a short bar joining their feet; then a stroke down the left that turns right along the bottom. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "去世 (qùshì) is built from 去 'to leave' and 世 (shì) 'the world', both inherited from Middle Chinese, khjoH and syejH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to leave' and the second 'a generation'. The sense 'the world' is not given there."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
